ASSISTANT **Changed files**
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT - `harness/planner.py` — policy-derived missing inputs (required → material → applicable conditional-material, with the exact pinned `distance_km` condition only; anything else is contract drift → `TerminalError`); transactional exactly-one-match school resolution with staged/committed IDs, preflight recording, explicit-ID bypass and conflict detection; Unicode-safe selector normalization with the single pinned alias (`teaching staff` → `teaching_fte`) and field routing (`metrics`/`ratios`/`grades`) from the registry `metric_list` and the input-catalog schema mapping/enums; a dependency-free draft-2020-12-subset validator over the registered pinned request schemas (registered-path-only loading); VC-POC-09/10 explicit-filter enforcement; and origin-aware `bad_request` handling (caller identity → clarification; otherwise → `TerminalError`).
ASSISTANT - `run.py` — the default CLI now calls `converse(None, deps, ...)` and no longer imports or builds the legacy agent; `converse()` retains explicit-agent support; credentials, rendering, exit codes and clarification limits unchanged.
ASSISTANT - `tests/unit/test_planner.py` — all named acceptance tests plus transactional-resolution, normalization, exact-request, constraint and error-origin coverage; the obsolete first-match and `bad_request → out_of_scope` tests were replaced.
ASSISTANT - `tests/unit/test_intent_boundary.py` — adds `test_planner_failure_is_not_unsupported` and planner-boundary tests (clarification bypasses narration/answer view; exact validated request reaches evidence; unnormalizable metrics and invalid explicit identities stay clarifications).
ASSISTANT - `tests/unit/test_run_cli.py` — adds `test_main_uses_pipeline_path_by_default` and a source-level no-legacy-agent check; all legacy-loop tests unchanged.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT **Checks performed**: reviewed every supplied acceptance id against the implementation and the named test node IDs against the test files. I could not execute the test suite (no shell access in this session), so the acceptance commands in the contract (`.venv/bin/python -m pytest ...`) have not been run by me and remain for the harness's verification steps.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT **Unresolved requirements / risks to verify on first run**:
ASSISTANT 1. The `ask()` pipeline is expected to let `TerminalError` propagate (the plan states planner failures propagate); if `harness/agent.py` catches it, `test_planner_failure_is_not_unsupported` will surface that and `harness/agent.py` (read-only here) would need a look.
ASSISTANT 2. Request validation uses a self-contained draft-2020-12-subset validator covering the keywords the generated v0.3 schemas use; if any pinned schema uses a keyword outside that subset, validation would under-check rather than mis-reject (safe direction), but worth confirming against all 16 schemas.
ASSISTANT 3. `request_scope_problem` semantics (in read-only `harness/tools.py`) are reused unchanged; the existing empty-`user_question` behaviour is assumed to be a no-op as today.
ASSISTANT 4. The stub emitter's directory search must return exactly one record per fixture school for pipeline-path resolution; legacy-path behaviour is untouched.
