USER harness/agent.py
USER ````
USER """Agent assembly: provider wiring, the output union, the rendering gate, budgets.
USER 
USER What this module is responsible for, and nothing else:
USER 
USER - **Provider wiring.** The local POC defaults to the token-backed Claude Code
USER   subscription account; the Anthropic SDK remains an explicit, potentially
USER   metered transport. SDK retries are 0 —
USER   `harness.retry` is the single retry owner (ADR-003).
USER - **The output union.** The model chooses between `AnswerDraft`,
USER   `ClarificationNeeded` and `Unsupported`; `ask()` widens that to
USER   `HarnessOutput` by attaching the preserved envelope fields and by adding the
USER   `BudgetExceeded` branch the model can never select (architecture §5).
USER - **The rendering gate.** An output validator applies `harness.rendering` and
USER   hands violations back as `ModelRetry`, so a run self-corrects rather than
USER   returning something the eval suite would fail later.
USER - **The control envelope.** `UsageLimits` for steps and tool calls, one wall-clock
USER   DEADLINE for the whole call, and measured spend checked between steps; a breach
USER   returns a typed `BudgetExceeded`, never a crash (ADR-004).
USER - **Telemetry.** One JSONL line per LLM request and one per run, written whether
USER   the run answered or tripped a budget (ADR-005) — a run that costs money and
USER   reports nothing is the one you most need the record of.
USER 
USER The system prompt is the FROZEN file `prompts/system.md`, read byte-exact by
USER `harness.prompt` and generated from `contract/` by `prompts/build_prompt.py`
USER (ADR-006). Nothing request-scoped is interpolated into it, and instructions are
USER marked cacheable when the real Anthropic provider is in use.
USER 
USER ## The two paths
USER 
USER `build_agent()` + old `ask(agent, deps, question, ...)` — the legacy tool-loop
USER path. Tests and eval replay that script a `FunctionModel` use this path. It is
USER kept intact for backward compatibility.
USER 
USER New `ask(deps, question, ...)` (no `agent` argument) — the 4-stage pipeline:
USER 1. `interpret_intent()` — LLM, no tools → StructuredIntent
USER 2. `plan_and_execute()` — deterministic → envelope or typed refusal
USER 3. `build_answer_view()` — deterministic → AnswerView
USER 4. `narrate()` — LLM, no tools → NarrationOutput
USER """
USER 
USER from __future__ import annotations
USER 
USER import asyncio
USER import logging
USER from datetime import datetime, timezone
USER from typing import Any
