ASSISTANT """Stage 2 — deterministic planner tests.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT Proves that `plan_and_execute()` branches purely on the intent, the pinned
ASSISTANT contract artefacts, and the evidence client's responses: no model calls, no
ASSISTANT guessing. Covered here:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT - derived required/material/conditional inputs (the model's missing-input
ASSISTANT   claim is never trusted), in pinned policy order;
ASSISTANT - transactional exactly-one-match school resolution (zero, ambiguous,
ASSISTANT   duplicate, conflicting and consistent identities; no partial Deps mutation);
ASSISTANT - selector normalization, pinned aliases, routing (`metrics` vs `ratios` vs
ASSISTANT   `grades`) and exact request dictionaries;
ASSISTANT - pinned-schema validation and VC-POC-09/10 explicit-filter constraints,
ASSISTANT   all failing closed before dispatch;
ASSISTANT - origin-aware evidence errors: caller-supplied identity bad_request
ASSISTANT   clarifies; planner/contract drift and operational stops are TerminalError.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT Three kinds of evidence client:
ASSISTANT - stub_client() — the real stub emitter (happy path with real fixture data)
ASSISTANT - _ErrorClient / _HappyClient — simple mocks for error/happy branch tests
ASSISTANT - _DirectoryClient — a directory-backed mock for identity-resolution tests
ASSISTANT """
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT from __future__ import annotations
ASSISTANT 
