ASSISTANT """Stage 2 of the 4-stage pipeline: deterministic planning and execution.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT `plan_and_execute()` takes a StructuredIntent and returns either:
ASSISTANT - a dict (the evidence envelope) — the happy path
ASSISTANT - ClarificationNeeded — an input the caller must supply or correct
ASSISTANT - Unsupported — an exclusion or an unknown question
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT No model calls. Every branch is a pure function of the intent, the pinned
ASSISTANT contract artefacts, and the evidence client's responses.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT What Stage 2 now guarantees (work item 20260908T113118):
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT - Required, material, and applicable conditional-material inputs are derived
ASSISTANT   from the pinned question policy and the assembled request. The intent
ASSISTANT   model's `missing_material_inputs` claim is never trusted.
ASSISTANT - Named schools resolve through the pinned directory and must match exactly
ASSISTANT   one record each. IDs are staged in mention order, deduplicated without
ASSISTANT   reordering, and committed to `Deps` only after every mention resolves; a
ASSISTANT   zero or ambiguous match clarifies with no evidence call and no partial
ASSISTANT   identity mutation. Caller-supplied numeric IDs bypass the preflight (the
ASSISTANT   bounded resolution of the pinned Definition-Pack conflict) and any conflict
ASSISTANT   with name-resolved identities fails closed before dispatch.
ASSISTANT - Selector labels are Unicode-case-folded and separator-normalized, matched
ASSISTANT   against pinned static vocabularies (registry `metric_list` where declared;
ASSISTANT   otherwise the input-catalog schema's field mapping and embedded enums), and
ASSISTANT   routed to the question's own request field: `metrics` for VC-POC-01/04/11,
ASSISTANT   `ratios` for VC-POC-03, `grades` for VC-POC-02/07. Unsupplied selectors are
ASSISTANT   omitted — the emitter keeps default ownership (no invented defaults).
ASSISTANT - Every request is validated against its registered pinned per-question
ASSISTANT   schema before dispatch. A planner-produced request that cannot satisfy its
ASSISTANT   schema raises TerminalError — planner defects are never dressed up as
ASSISTANT   Unsupported user outcomes.
ASSISTANT - Error origins are separated: a bad_request against a request whose school
ASSISTANT   identity was caller-supplied is an identity clarification; any other
ASSISTANT   bad_request after deterministic validation is planner/contract drift and
ASSISTANT   raises TerminalError. excluded/unknown/unanswerable keep their typed
ASSISTANT   abstentions; data_unavailable/internal remain operational stops.
ASSISTANT """
